00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Wax your balls...

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.600
"You wax your balls?"

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.200
...and prepare to get the crap kicked out of you,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.460
because we have the worst wedding anniversary ever.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.160
Yes, Black Mirror is back with a surprisingly happy ending.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.740
"Mind if I finish myself off?"

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.940
In this video, we'll be taking a deep dive into the Striking Vipers ending,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.060
as well as some of the episode's Easter eggs.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.040
So if you want to jump right to the Easter eggs, I've left a timestamp in the description.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.350
At its core, Striking Vipers is the story of Danny, a middle-aged family man

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.940
who must come to terms with his own sexuality.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.960
At the beginning of the episode, he's filled with passion,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.360
role-playing with his girlfriend at the bar and having sex with her on the counter of their bathroom.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.419
Their relationship is strong and you can tell these two are deeply into each other.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.580
It's not until 11 years later that Danny's perfect life isn't all it's...

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.420
cracked up to be?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.740
Even though he has the American dream; a house in the suburbs, doting wife and child,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.010
he still longs for something more.

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:54.749
Staring at multiple women like the one at his birthday party,

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.802
and another from across the street.

00:00:56.802 --> 00:01:00.220
The passion that Danny and Theo used to have is gone,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.340
and part of him still yearns for that.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.140
Their sex life today is mechanical; timed out on an app and regulated

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.460
to increase their chances of having another baby.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.796
Theo calls Danny out on this, saying:

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.760
"You don't touch me anymore."

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.480
"Theo..."
"You don't even kiss me."

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.540
Not to mention how many times Danny uses the "I'm too tired" excuse

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.549
to avoid having sex with his wife.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:24.570
This has an adverse effect on Theo, who questions if she's good enough.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.740
She checks her body out in the mirror as if trying to see what's wrong with her.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.850
She herself looks at others making out, remembering when she used to be like that.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:36.149
But unlike Danny, Theo doesn't give in to these temptations.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.799
Even when she's approached at the bar by another man, as she later tells Danny:

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.304
"Partnerships are about commitment, and you need to make sacrifices in order for it to work."

00:01:46.304 --> 00:01:48.060
Which leads us to Danny and Karl.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:53.220
Karl gets Danny, for his birthday, an immersive new video game called Striking Vipers [X],

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.520
in which each player is brought into the game using state-of-the-art VR technology.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.040
At first, Danny loves this.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.014
His knee, which he damaged years ago, isn't a problem here.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.080
The same can't be said with his feelings for Karl.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.300
Striking Vipers is also a metaphor for Danny and Karl's desires,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:13.460
which is contrasted with Tetris; whereas Tetris is cookie-cutter and Karl calls it "boring",

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.780
having to fit pieces into a set box,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.960
Striking Vipers is exciting, sexy and raw.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.440
This acts as a juxtaposition between Danny's real world and fantasy world.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.380
Over the next few months, the two men continue their affair,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.059
which only causes more damage to Danny and Theo's relationship.

00:02:30.059 --> 00:02:34.229
Danny even forgets about his wedding anniversary, as Theo says about Danny:

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.410
"I mean, you shrivel away."

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.880
"You go inside...

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.270
leave me on the outside."

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:45.660
Danny has now quenched his desire for passion at the expense of his relationship with Theo,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:49.960
and things continue to get worse as Karl and Danny fall deeper in love with each other.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.200
The same is true with Karl and his relationship with Mariella.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.480
The first scene with the two of them sets up that they probably aren't meant for each other.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:57.980
I mean, come on.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.961
She doesn't even know who Dennis Rodman is.

00:02:59.961 --> 00:03:01.180
Later on in the episode,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.880
Karl can't even get it up when he's with her.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.500
He's in love with Danny, which begs the question:

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.960
Is it cheating?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.180
When Danny tells Karl he can no longer see him, Karl tries to convince him it's not,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.620
saying "it's no different than watching porn".

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.840
But Danny doesn't really buy it, and I don't either.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.440
When Karl tries to get Danny back,

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.660
he tells him how he experimented with other people in the game.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.320
Even other people who played the same avatar as him, Lance.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.480
For Karl, it wasn't the character he was attracted to; it was the man behind it, Danny.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.420
The same can also be said for Danny.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.300
He sends a message to Karl with the X kiss symbol,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.600
and he's the one to suggest they kiss at the end to see if what they have is real.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.700
If Danny was just into it because he was attracted to the character of Roxette,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.060
he would never have done those things.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.600
Danny and Karl fight it out, which is pretty much two dudes releasing months of sexual frustration.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.220
They have, in essence, become Striking Vipers

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.080
only this time, they're not fighting in a game world.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.905
Danny is picked up by Theo at the police station and question in the car

00:04:00.905 --> 00:04:03.600
about what exactly is going on between him and Karl,

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.430
before it cuts to black and we fast forward to Danny's 40th birthday.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.940
Remember at the beginning, we were celebrating Danny's 38th,

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.920
so some time has passed.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.150
Now, we never really know what Danny told Theo,

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.520
But the next few scenes suggest that he told her the truth,

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.200
and have since come to an agreement.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:25.080
For his birthday, Danny can fulfil his online fun with Karl without any of the secrets and hurt,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.418
while Theo can hook up with randoms at the bar.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.149
They both exchange symbols of this new trust.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.560
Theo gives Danny his VR set and Danny gives her wedding box,

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.280
so that she'll have somewhere to put a ring when she goes out to the bar.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.260
They both tell each other that they have to give it back in the morning.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.680
Now, it's uncertain whether this is just for Danny's birthday or if this is a monthly thing,

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.840
but it's definitely a step in the right direction.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.140
Although this episode deals a lot with sexuality,

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.720
It's really about honesty and communication,

00:04:52.721 --> 00:04:57.239
and how other relationships are hurt by not being open about how we truly feel.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.400
It's only when Danny is fully honest with Theo that their relationship can heal,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.120
and they can once again be passionate with each other.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.900
And now on to the fun part, where we pick apart

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.720
some of the Black Mirror Easter eggs found in this episode.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.500
Striking Vipers is directed by Owen Harris, who previously directed

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.660
Black Mirror episodes Be Right Back and San Junipero,

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:19.950
and there are quite a few nods to San Junipero in this episode.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:23.940
For example, the company that makes the VR set is TCKR,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.080
the same company responsible for uploading peoples' consciousness to the cloud in San Junipero.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.720
The VR set also looks similar to those used in that episode as well.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.920
TCKR, although not confirmed, is likely an offshoot of Bandersnatch's Tuckersoft,

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.860
founded by Mohan Tucker.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.520
Tucker is also seen as trending in the next episode Smithereens,

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.280
along with SaitoGemu, which is the company that makes Striking Vipers.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.600
Speaking of Striking Vipers, we have two versions of the game:

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.460
The original which Karl and Danny play at the beginning,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.660
and Striking Vipers X, or the Roman numeral for 10,

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.860
which takes place eleven years later.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:01.280
So it's safe to assume there have been at least 10 different versions of this game;

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.420
one for each year that has passed since the boys first started playing.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:10.480
In the game, we get a reference to Tundra, a white bear just like the episode titled White Bear,

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:15.280
and a level called Saito Helipad, which Carl and Danny appear on in the last shot of the episode.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.760
You'll also notice, as the camera zooms out,

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.460
the image of Striking Vipers on the side of the building.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.240
Danny also gets a gift of Lacie chocolate;

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.020
Lacie, the main character from Nosedive.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.430
And is it just me or does this character here look a bit like the Bandersnatch monster?

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:34.169
All right guys, not a lot of whole Easter eggs in this episode, but I hope you enjoyed the video.

